-    
-    <h2>3. Recording of data on our website</h2>
-    <p><strong>Cookies</strong></p>
-    <p>In some instances, our website and its pages use so-called cookies. Cookies do not cause any damage to your computer and do not contain viruses. The purpose of cookies is to make our website more user friendly, effective and more secure. Cookies are small text files that are placed on your computer and stored by your browser.</p>
+<LegalLayout title="Privacy Notice">
+    <p>This is a demonstration news site. Use made-up account details and never reuse a password from another service.</p>
+
+    <h2>Account forms</h2>
+    <p>Sign-up and sign-in require only a username and password. We do not ask for your real name, email address, date of birth, or marketing preferences. Your details are sent over HTTPS only when you submit the form.</p>
+    <p>The recipient is the demo account service hosted on Google Cloud Functions at <code>us-central1-web-devrel-apps.cloudfunctions.net</code> (the <code>times_cdn/api/register</code> and <code>times_cdn/api/login</code> endpoints). It uses the submitted details to create or check an account and receives network information such as your IP address. The account request omits browser cookies and the referring page URL.</p>
+    <p>The forms do not save credentials or returned tokens in local storage, session storage, or cookies. Password fields are cleared after each request completes. Your browser or password manager may separately offer to save your details, under your control. This demo displays the account service's result; it does not establish a persistent signed-in session.</p>
+
+    <h2>Third parties and browsing</h2>
+    <p>The shared page layout does not load analytics, advertising scripts, or remotely hosted fonts. No optional tracking is enabled, so there is no tracking consent to grant or withdraw.</p>
+    <p>Some articles contain externally hosted images. Viewing those images connects your browser to the image host, which receives connection information such as your IP address. Pages use a no-referrer policy to avoid sending the page URL with those requests. Following an external link takes you to a service with its own privacy practices.</p>
+
+    <h2>Reading lists and technical data</h2>
+    <p>Saving an article can store its identifier in a server-side reading list associated with a session cookie. The shared layout does not create a reading-list session just for visiting a page. You can remove saved articles using the reading-list controls and clear site cookies in your browser to remove its session identifier.</p>
+    <p>The site host and account service may process request metadata in their operational logs. Their logging, credential storage, retention periods, and deletion procedures cannot be verified from this site's source code. Do not submit sensitive or real-world account information.</p>
+
+    <h2>Retention and questions</h2>
+    <p>Clearing a form or your browser data does not delete an account held by the external account service. This demo does not provide an account deletion control or a verified privacy contact. Before using it with real personal data, the operator must provide retention periods, deletion and access procedures, and a working contact. See the <a href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}legal/imprint`}>imprint</a> for the demo's background.</p>
 </LegalLayout>
